         Question
  There is a critical issue going on with the Nautilus application in Stratos DC. The production support team identified that the application is unable to connect to the database. After digging into the issue, the team found that mariadb service is down on the database server.

         Solution
  
    1-login into the data server
      ssh user@host
    2- look at the mariaDB logs
       tail -f /var/log/mariadb.log
    3- check the status
      sudo systemctl status mariadb
       . if it makes permission failes/down do the following
    4- set ownership
      sudo chown -R mysql:mysql /var/run/mariadb
    5- set the permission
      sudo chown 755 /var/run/mariadb
    6- restart service
      sudo systemctl restart mariadb
       . Check status to see if it's had restarted 
